 be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=15.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{3(1-{15}^{N})}{1-15} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{14}(1-{15}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{14}({15}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-5259/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5259"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-67076/selection/966e9581c5613db124895690c18670670d24db984d2b932b800a18c429af1df0" :answer/id #uuid "fbc1230d-2569-5a93-be64-c28688bfcbc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}({2}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67076/selection/e456e546dfc35df250c981ae03f514f48212ab0caa41387724dc4a92cf01f977" :answer/id #uuid "a7088325-3b04-5187-9260-05f3e4bfa2c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}(1-{2}^{N})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67076/selection/fa104ae6a77997041acf2c90406063697a2b905747848464b819fa1451230c2a" :answer/id #uuid "e2bb982d-2b3e-52df-981b-19cf2fa244d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(1-{2}^{N})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67076/selection/cd4ed5dbbdc12300f368166d50880658909c30581f8aa7884759fb3522cbb6d1" :answer/id #uuid "2623b495-2163-560b-9420-399fb25b62e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5({2}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67076/selection/e7d965d89c08ea3b2cf9c16ba6f4e8855ecf87ce1329dd6524849fa5d7da1587" :answer/id #uuid "9883df09-b52a-5c30-b592-950e574c87a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{10}^{N}-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67076/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6087a1a3-63fb-5eb7-9a81-4fcbb5c04673" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-67076/selection/cd4ed5dbbdc12300f368166d50880658909c30581f8aa7884759fb3522cbb6d1" :answer-field/choices ["q-67076/selection/966e9581c5613db124895690c18670670d24db984d2b932b800a18c429af1df0" "q-67076/selection/e456e546dfc35df250c981ae03f514f48212ab0caa41387724dc4a92cf01f977" "q-67076/selection/fa104ae6a77997041acf2c90406063697a2b905747848464b819fa1451230c2a" "q-67076/selection/cd4ed5dbbdc12300f368166d50880658909c30581f8aa7884759fb3522cbb6d1" "q-67076/selection/e7d965d89c08ea3b2cf9c16ba6f4e8855ecf87ce1329dd6524849fa5d7da1587"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-67076" :question/id #uuid "857472c7-6a76-5f57-84e0-8d959995ee62" :question/math-academy-id "q-67076" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $5$ and the common ratio is $2?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=2.$ Therefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-5(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =5({2}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-67076/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-67076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276476/field-1/0f0ffaf46c608d40e4b4c68238dada56a64cd7defd4ecc4289d580e309465162" :answer/id #uuid "93d305e8-f5f1-5174-97d7-8104d428e529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(3^N-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276476/field-1/b0b9cf2d9927f4bf87d6d86393f4e69625aa43ba43d0a1fb59dde4a111e04f69" :answer/id #uuid "326f28e6-12de-54e9-bfce-d498825f326c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(3^N+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276476/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee4dadc8-1e84-521b-a273-2addeb0ddbdc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276476/field-1/0f0ffaf46c608d40e4b4c68238dada56a64cd7defd4ecc4289d580e309465162" :answer-field/choices ["q-276476/field-1/0f0ffaf46c608d40e4b4c68238dada56a64cd7defd4ecc4289d580e309465162" "q-276476/field-1/b0b9cf2d9927f4bf87d6d86393f4e69625aa43ba43d0a1fb59dde4a111e04f69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276476" :question/id #uuid "e57a29f2-809a-5f43-832e-20ee9d5d19d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-276476" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $8$ and the common ratio is $3?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=8$ and $r=3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{8(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =4({3}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-276476/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276476"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110166/selection/aad5e5a8d90fc8226ba874440a829eb5ca16d95756de1b1810d5761df8b035a4" :answer/id #uuid "133396cc-2531-5640-918a-487469d5bfbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3({3}^{-N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110166/selection/7b1f235bea504a6b0953b4b75c5184ba980982011e60d7339c7e59832aa1afbf" :answer/id #uuid "f37b9806-5c64-5cdf-84b2-357f8c4c475e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4({4}^{-N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110166/selection/5b296f4aa288d563d4739911c0a8262064121e57540e691c655005b044777388" :answer/id #uuid "59e7aeff-cb57-53a1-a8aa-f73272eaa46e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}({4}^{-N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110166/selection/14527e6628af1669bb4ffd0b553b84439754624c9ed9671b2b0139d4f44bf04d" :answer/id #uuid "a41f66c9-f9cd-5cb9-b21e-e7610d1c4a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({4}^{-N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110166/selection/05690293044cb5b2669d6fb0a19d7174f13df30bec75447df8605f9d790e34d3" :answer/id #uuid "0ac5aa50-0c14-5498-9e9d-13edf124dc35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}({3}^{-N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110166/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90f80dc0-083f-50e5-882c-e4c135b4d07c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110166/selection/7b1f235bea504a6b0953b4b75c5184ba980982011e60d7339c7e59832aa1afbf" :answer-field/choices ["q-110166/selection/aad5e5a8d90fc8226ba874440a829eb5ca16d95756de1b1810d5761df8b035a4" "q-110166/selection/7b1f235bea504a6b0953b4b75c5184ba980982011e60d7339c7e59832aa1afbf" "q-110166/selection/5b296f4aa288d563d4739911c0a8262064121e57540e691c655005b044777388" "q-110166/selection/14527e6628af1669bb4ffd0b553b84439754624c9ed9671b2b0139d4f44bf04d" "q-110166/selection/05690293044cb5b2669d6fb0a19d7174f13df30bec75447df8605f9d790e34d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110166" :question/id #uuid "6a880b7a-8ca5-52a7-8783-3b205cea8268" :question/math-academy-id "q-110166" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{1}{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=-3$ and $r=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =-4[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}] \\\\  & =4[{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}-1] \\\\  & =4({4}^{-N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110166/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110166"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276481/field-1/262d8dc224653ffc1b6a1cd2cdc78a9eec92872fa2f1d9f1daa7952f00bec502" :answer/id #uuid "a3041515-0f9d-5c86-8a43-ef97d983f10b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(2^N-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276481/field-1/345b9950b5fef59f9336dd606207a4934f9b6f507419b390a9dc7a9c8443d633" :answer/id #uuid "de5aff5a-b6d9-523b-92b8-e59e381f1a8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5(2^N+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276481/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0793865-dda4-58f5-944f-71bf872b9b33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276481/field-1/262d8dc224653ffc1b6a1cd2cdc78a9eec92872fa2f1d9f1daa7952f00bec502" :answer-field/choices ["q-276481/field-1/262d8dc224653ffc1b6a1cd2cdc78a9eec92872fa2f1d9f1daa7952f00bec502" "q-276481/field-1/345b9950b5fef59f9336dd606207a4934f9b6f507419b390a9dc7a9c8443d633"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276481" :question/id #uuid "c2eb0daf-a508-5ea3-8ad9-3a68146465db" :question/math-academy-id "q-276481" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $5+10+20+⋯?$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=2.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-5(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =5({2}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-276481/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276481"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276482/field-1/238d35f515f22014399e34c83677f869b70eada62f4bce583a340f406b15e2e2" :answer/id #uuid "b4de5897-78b7-52f8-98fa-d0fbf3194f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(3^N-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276482/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "73b662cd-3dcc-5b05-8e2e-79d93866cd68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276482/field-1/238d35f515f22014399e34c83677f869b70eada62f4bce583a340f406b15e2e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-276482/field-1/238d35f515f22014399e34c83677f869b70eada62f4bce583a340f406b15e2e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276482" :question/id #uuid "cac3a52a-4ec7-51c8-87df-4a1dd61e0e9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-276482" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $6+18+54+⋯?$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=3.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =3({3}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-276482/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276482"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-270557/field-1/89776b293f888e50956ba9e019d1390b7df802f56c7a96bc45330ca1a52eba9a" :answer/id #uuid "26f1bf3c-196e-5832-88b4-c1f6d2d4909b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}(6^N-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270557/field-1/3862697c514f3a7e1032b5a7a1a40247c850c7ef5ab29fa48d90e8ab74d953b7" :answer/id #uuid "8dfa61f3-c6e0-57a5-b9f5-2123aa077f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}(6^N+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270557/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dbffc279-c38d-5246-a3ed-9f0c6e17c348" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-270557/field-1/89776b293f888e50956ba9e019d1390b7df802f56c7a96bc45330ca1a52eba9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-270557/field-1/89776b293f888e50956ba9e019d1390b7df802f56c7a96bc45330ca1a52eba9a" "q-270557/field-1/3862697c514f3a7e1032b5a7a1a40247c850c7ef5ab29fa48d90e8ab74d953b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-270557" :question/id #uuid "0e583e3c-68ff-5a26-a404-3d96c2b20a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-270557" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $7+42+252+\\,⋯?$ Express your answer as a function of $N.$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{7} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=7$ and $r=6.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\