$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{4(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-4(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =4({2}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110180/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110180"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276485/field-1/edee3a3056d054fc391f7187445860635f7bba2aae041a93c02793bf6078f015" :answer/id #uuid "2834e98b-10d6-5b2f-83e2-8210fde5b77f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6(3^N-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276485/field-1/74bbd0095de82b815a870d9c396b182d8af2393df9c852682f82027349fc3f2e" :answer/id #uuid "79b80505-54ad-53ca-a7c8-0232754ec326" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6(3^N+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276485/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c36a8833-b87c-501a-820d-f54641a91a20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276485/field-1/edee3a3056d054fc391f7187445860635f7bba2aae041a93c02793bf6078f015" :answer-field/choices ["q-276485/field-1/edee3a3056d054fc391f7187445860635f7bba2aae041a93c02793bf6078f015" "q-276485/field-1/74bbd0095de82b815a870d9c396b182d8af2393df9c852682f82027349fc3f2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276485" :question/id #uuid "2a03e1d4-3899-53ba-b621-6a814f66aa1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-276485" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $324$ and the common ratio is $3?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 324 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 324 & =27{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=12$ and $r=3.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{12(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(1-{3}^{N})}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-6(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =6({3}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-276485/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276485"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277872/field-1/9dbbc21e2a545b7e3e8872a90fe00b245a173a475406761b2fc9c4f587cede41" :answer/id #uuid "d42e3474-809a-50b4-84bd-071d38310aba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8(2^N-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277872/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "632de4db-342a-5a66-9c88-aa31c1466dc3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277872/field-1/9dbbc21e2a545b7e3e8872a90fe00b245a173a475406761b2fc9c4f587cede41" :answer-field/choices ["q-277872/field-1/9dbbc21e2a545b7e3e8872a90fe00b245a173a475406761b2fc9c4f587cede41"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277872" :question/id #uuid "cad8ab82-cf5f-5932-b397-22a270d16a6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-277872" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $7$th term is $512$ and the common ratio is $2?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 512 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {2}^{(7-1)} \\\\ 512 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=8$ and $r=2.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{8(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8(1-{2}^{N})}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-8(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =8({2}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-277872/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-67090/selection/7939af287bd6169cd0c63d9ed1a39ce0670910a8c4b4b7f682c720d074bfffee" :answer/id #uuid "b7a2ed4d-7aa1-56f1-a45e-d82c3096ee54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(1-{4}^{N})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67090/selection/daefde542bed6914ddc410983f31d582b23ebd8abb79714c5597829aeb094b33" :answer/id #uuid "82a6f3eb-c1d8-5977-9184-27bae9faa616" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4({2}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67090/selection/5293563bb36bbe32e37d6ef478676e9fa175bf61d3e411246fc6b71a462b3452" :answer/id #uuid "a80d60c2-bbd0-59a9-b2e0-af71f293481b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{4}^{N}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67090/selection/02e15e135c002742ff01eb7c77132bf53c11e1725e6a76bbf4f603103049e8ea" :answer/id #uuid "e13c7082-47c0-5bb6-8c05-5d4cbae7c70d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{2}^{N}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67090/selection/ea09f8e0da298ff94ac951995b30f3a833b0294590ed6836aa328569bab048d2" :answer/id #uuid "09ee468a-a885-582e-8a83-45e198750598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(1-{2}^{N})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67090/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "67a70615-3d1c-5554-83aa-cd139d678e64" :answer-field/key "selection" :